system partition may have two partition since android 8.0, and compatible to project treble for only flash Generic System Images to upgrade android system,

fastboot flash system GSI.img

do not specify system_a or system_b, fastboot will flash on the active slot, 
fastboot getvar all  # can get which slot is active

fastboot --disable-verity --disable-verification flash vbmeta_b vbmeta_patched.img  # disable verified boot metadata
fastboot erase system_b  # fastboot erase system_a
fastboot flash system_b GSI.img # fastboot flash system_a GSI.img
fastboot set_active b # change active slot 
fastboot erase cache
fastboot -w reboot    # -w will clean data

# if the device can not boot, revert to the other slot
fastboot set_active b

boot(kernel ramdisk), system(android system), vendor(driver), vbmeta(verified boot metadata)
dtbo(Device Tree Blob Overlay, config for hardware)
data(data and apps), cache(temporary file), metadata(slot information)

# dump origin vbmeta
fastboot dump vbmeta vbmeta_backup.img
# or extract it from the official fastboot package, copy boot.img and vbmeta.img to a.tar, 
# magisk 'install' -> 'install to file' choose a.tar, it will generate patched vbmeta.img and boot.img

fastboot flash vbmeta magisk_patched_vbmeta.img

# or use avbtool
pip3 install avbtool
avbtool make_vbmeta_image --flag 2 --output vbmeta_patched.img


The A/B partition scheme divides critical Android partitions (e.g., system, boot, vendor, vbmeta) into two sets, referred to as slot A and slot B. Each slot contains a complete, independent copy of the Android system, allowing updates to be applied to one slot while the other remains active.

Slot A: system_a, boot_a, vendor_a, vbmeta_a
Slot B: system_b, boot_b, vendor_b, vbmeta_b
Shared: data, cache, metadata

# get current active slot
adb shell getprop ro.boot.slot_suffix



